<!--
  iOS native sandbox declarations — Quadrant I obstacle: "Native Build
  Sandboxing Crashes".

  Paste these into ios/App/App/Info.plist AFTER running `npx cap add ios`.
  Missing any of these causes an immediate, silent crash the first time the
  corresponding hardware is touched — there is no JS-catchable error.

  Apple rejects vague usage strings. Each string below states who is asking,
  what is collected, and why.
-->

<key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
<string>PNSM uses your camera to take a verification selfie when you check in for your shift.</string>

<key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
<string>PNSM checks your location against your assigned office geofence to confirm your attendance when you check in.</string>

<!--
  ONLY required if background telemetry is approved and shipped.
  Do NOT add these until that decision is made: requesting Always
  authorisation without a demonstrable need is a common App Store rejection,
  and it materially changes the app's privacy posture.
-->
<key>NSLocationAlwaysAndWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
<string>PNSM records your location during your assigned shift hours so your employer can verify field attendance. Tracking is disabled outside your shift.</string>

<key>UIBackgroundModes</key>
<array>
  <string>location</string>
</array>
